# Laravel Code Quality

- Keep production code understandable before optimizing prematurely.
- Prefer explicit naming over clever abstractions.
- Avoid duplicated business rules.
- Keep comments focused on decisions and invariants, not obvious syntax.
- Add/update documentation when behavior changes.
- Do not bypass tests to make CI green.
- Do not weaken types or authorization merely to simplify implementation.
- Refactor repeated patterns into well-named abstractions only after a real duplication pattern appears.
- Every pull request should leave the codebase more consistent with the documented architecture.
